{
  "abstract": "Actual heterogeneous factorial-count identities, with repeated-index corrections, and the unconditional optimal 41/30 power for the third factorial cumulant. Absolute triple activity has the same upper exponent. The fourth-cumulant decomposition retains the positive compatible quartic mass and distinguishes 5/3 and 3/2 errors; the exact quadratic Poisson–Charlier approximation has matching 4/3 upper and lower power bounds.",
